# Dashboard Page Context

This page should make the user's operational context obvious before they interact with controls.

::page id=dashboard-home url="/dashboard"
  title="Analytics Dashboard"
  audience="new operators"
  goal="Help users understand live business health and find the next useful action."
  context="The page needs to foreground status, filters, and shareable reporting without making users decode the interface."

  ::tour id=dashboard-onboarding library=shepherd
    title="Dashboard Onboarding"
    description="Guides new users through key metrics and filters."
    options={"useModalOverlay":true}

    ::trigger type=url pattern="/dashboard" autoStart=true
    ::/trigger

    ::step id=welcome target=".hero" position=bottom order=1
      title="Welcome to your dashboard"
      body="This is where you see your live metrics."
    ::/step

    ::step id=filters target="#filter-panel" position=right order=2 options={"scrollTo":true}
      title="Filter your data"
      body="Use these filters to narrow what you see."
    ::/step
  ::/tour
::/page
